{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And every beast</b> Three times in the Masorah: החיה וכל בהמה, וכל בהמה, וכל בהמה מפרסת פרסה — to teach that the חיה (wild animal) is included in בהמה (beast), like there where it is written החיה וכל בהמה, and even a fetus, where it is written וכל בהמה מפרסת וגו׳ בבהמה אותה תאכלו — to include the fetus."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The three cited phrases are drawn from Leviticus 11:2–3 and Deuteronomy 14:4–6; the Ba'al HaTurim gives no verse addresses, so they are left unaddressed per convention."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:03.512376620Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}